Rule 1 (out tensor must have the same shape as input)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = ndim(v_2) ∧ if ndim(v_1) = 0 then true else ∀ i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) = shape(v_2, i)
>>
Rule 2 (out tensor must have a floating-point or complex dtype to store acosh results)
{v_2 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_2) = 6 ∨ dtype_(v_2) = 7 ∨ dtype_(v_2) = 8 ∨ dtype_(v_2) = 9 ∨ dtype_(v_2) = 10
>>
Rule 3 (complex input requires complex out)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= if (dtype_(v_1) = 9 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 10) then (dtype_(v_2) = 9 ∨ dtype_(v_2) = 10)
>>
Rule 4 (when input is floating or complex, out dtype matches input dtype)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= if (dtype_(v_1) = 6 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 7 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 8 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 9 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 10) then dtype_(v_2) = dtype_(v_1)
